# Environment and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Temporary files
.tmp/
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Credentials
credentials.json
token.json

# IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Node (if applicable)
node_modules/
dist/

# Python (if applicable)
venv/
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# Downloaded corpus and regenerable experiment artifacts stay out; measured
# results and the manifest that gives them provenance are the deliverable and
# are versioned. So is the Phase 3 selection: HU-3 asks for the choice of K to
# live in a versioned artifact, and a decision recorded in an ignored file is
# exactly the one the repository cannot reproduce.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
!data/manifest.json
!data/results/
data/results/*
!data/results/*.json
!data/selection/
data/selection/*
!data/selection/*.json
# The Phase 4 freeze, by the same rule as Phase 3's: every number of that phase is
# bound to it, so a checkout that cannot verify the digest cannot check the results.
!data/expansion/
data/expansion/*
!data/expansion/*.json
# The traces are diagnostics, not a freeze: 0.7 MB per arm of per-round detail. No
# `cer` stage writes them - they came from the Phase 4 report script, which is not in
# the repository (a gap declared in USER_GUIDE.md). The reading that matters is quoted
# in 4.results.md.
data/traces/
# Exploratory diagnostics quoted by a closure document. Small, and versioned for the
# same reason results are: a figure in a report must point at a file that exists.
!data/diagnostics/
data/diagnostics/*
!data/diagnostics/*.json
# Phase 5: the frozen pilot and the navigation run (hop run, traces, gate decision).
# Small and versioned, like every freeze and result before them. Both are full of
# content-hash unit ids, which is why .secrets.baseline excludes them by path (D12).
!data/pilot/
data/pilot/*
!data/pilot/*.json
!data/navigation/
data/navigation/*
!data/navigation/*.json
# The extraction sample report of Phase 5: the measured figures deviation 5.1 rests on.
# Only the report; the extraction archive's versioning is decided in T13 (plan D7).
!data/extraction/
data/extraction/*
!data/extraction/sample-report.json
# T13 (plan D7): the extraction archive is the non-reproducible record of what the pilot
# measured, versioned because it compresses to 2.5 MB; its summary carries the digest the
# archive is verified against. The batch state is operational and stays out.
!data/extraction/extraction-*.jsonl.gz
!data/extraction/extraction-*.json
# Phase 6 (plan D1, D20): the checks, the freeze, results, per-question outcomes, diagnostics,
# traces, readouts and the decision, flat in one directory and never under data/results/. Their
# deterministic hex ids are skipped by the content filter in .github/detect_secrets_filters.py,
# not by a path exclusion, so the scanner keeps reading everything else they hold.
!data/replacement/
data/replacement/*
!data/replacement/*.json

# Phase 7: cheap entity extraction.
# Keep the measured extraction record and evaluation artifacts; models and
# regenerable node-index files remain ignored. Every run-*.json a versioned
# artifact names in its `run_file` field is versioned too, so a checkout can
# open what dev.json and test.json point at.
!data/phase7/
data/phase7/*

!data/phase7/gliner/
data/phase7/gliner/*
!data/phase7/gliner/records.jsonl.gz
!data/phase7/gliner/extraction.json
!data/phase7/gliner/dev.json
!data/phase7/gliner/run-*.json

!data/phase7/spacy/
data/phase7/spacy/*
!data/phase7/spacy/records.jsonl.gz
!data/phase7/spacy/extraction.json
!data/phase7/spacy/dev.json
!data/phase7/spacy/run-*.json

!data/phase7/selection.json
!data/phase7/test.json

.cache/
models/
output/
*.npy
*.npz

# Python tooling
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Saved-webpage asset folders (js/css/images), not worth versioning
*_files/

# Reference material that is not part of the experiment: official PDFs and saved
# articles by third parties. Kept locally, never published.
docs/bases legales/

# Personal reading aid, in Spanish, for the Phase 3 vocabulary. The project
# documents in English by convention; this file is a deliberate local exception
# and is not part of the deliverable.
docs/GLOSARIO.md

# Configuration mirrors written by other agent tools. `.claude/` and `CLAUDE.md`
# are the only agent configuration this repository tracks; never publish a copy.
.agents/
.codex/
AGENTS.md
